Hi,

Wondering if anyone can suggest a solution for the following:
- render a different .html or .md file depending on user input;
-- i.e.

renderHTML('$filename.html'); renderMarkdown('$filename.md');

-- where $filename is defined by a widget, e.g. radio buttons <http://shiny.rstudio.com/gallery/widget-gallery.html>, from which:
(1) server.R receives input$radio and passes the value to ui.R;
(2) ui.R then renders the appropriate file.

I can achieve (1) of course, and ui.R will print the "value" received from server.R, but I cannot figure out (2): how to pass "value" to renderHTML() or renderMarkdown. Can anyone help? I've tried out Dynamic UI and Reactive Programming but these haven't led me to the solution; perhaps this is the right track though?

many thanks, Andrew

Reproducible example below:

##ui.R

library(markdown)

shinyUI(fluidPage(
  radioButtons("radio", label = h3("Radio buttons"),
   choices = list("Choice 1" = "foo1.md", "Choice 2" = "foo2.md"), selected = "foo1.md"),
  hr(),
  fluidRow(column(3,
    verbatimTextOutput("value"),
    includeMarkdown(textOutput("value"))  # same outcome with verbatimTextOutput()
  ))
))

##server.R

shinyServer(function(input, output) {
  output$value <- renderPrint({ input$radio })  # same outcome with renderText()
})

Markdown files can be something trivial like:
## foo1
* Hello, World! from foo1.md

## foo2
* Hello, World! from foo1.md

If I run this Shiny App, the error message is as follows: "invalid 'description' argument"

