I have an app which serves up data from a database in graphical and summary form.  The data are from monitoring sites and the online sites and the parameters measured at each site varies.  I have taken an approach used elsewhere using call and do.call to generate the UI.  My question is, can I use the dynamically created input elements in an observe or reactive construct and have the code respond when any of the elements changes?

In the example below, stns is populated with the available monitoirng stations and the UI built with a navbarpanel with one panelset for each site.  Within each panelset I have a dateRangeInput and tabset.  Each of the these have a dynamic name.  The crux of the matter is that I would like to update the data set based on changes in the dateRangeInput.  I have not been able to get the observe or reactive construct to recognize changes in the dynamically named dateRangeInputs.  Is this possible?

shinyUI(
  fluidPage(
    uiOutput('navUI')
  )
)

#get the online stations from the db - db left out for example purposes
stns<-list(stn1=NULL,stn2=NULL,stn3=NULL)

shinyServer(function(input, output) {

  output$navUI<-renderUI({
    ## Dynamically render Navbarpanel based on the available stations
    do.call("navbarPage",
            args=c(theme='journal.css',title='Water Quality Monitoring Stations',id='navBar',
                   #create tabPanel entry for each station returned as active
                   lapply(names(stns),function(s){
                     call("tabPanel",title=s,
                          #create sidebar layout
                          call('sidebarLayout',
                               #create sidebar panel with header/title, dateRangeInput and current data table
                               call('sidebarPanel',width=3,#c(
                                    call('imageOutput',paste0('image_',s)),
                                    call('htmlOutput',paste0('head_',s)),
                                    do.call('dateRangeInput',
                                            list(inputId=paste0('daysx_',s),
                                                 label='X Axis Range',
                                                 min=as.POSIXct('2014-05-01'),
                                                 max=now,
                                                 start=now-60*60*24*2,
                                                 end=now)),
                                    call('tableOutput',paste0("table_",s))#)
                               ),
                               #create main panel call
                               call('mainPanel',
                                    #create tabset
                                    call('tabsetPanel',id=paste0('tabSet_',s),
                                         #create tab for plots
                                         call("tabPanel","Plot",value=paste0("plot_",s),
                                              call('uiOutput',paste0("ggvis_",s))
                                         ),
                                         #create tab for summary
                                         call("tabPanel","Summary",value=paste0("summary_",s),
                                              call('tableOutput',paste0("summary_",s))
                                         ),
                                         #create tab for map
                                         call("tabPanel","Map",value=paste0('map_',s),
                                              call('imageOutput',paste0('map_',s))
                                         )
                                    )
                               )
                          )
                     )
                   }
                   )
            )
    )
  })

#here is where my question lies
# i want to call a function update.data when any of the dateRangeInput change
dat<-observe({
  x<-isolate(input$navBar)
  update.data(x,time.rng=input[[paste0('daysx_',x)]])
})

