Robin,

These are my observations, running your application locally, and also on shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io>:

- Locally I see a delay of 22-30 s initially to load the map. Is it much faster on your system? If yes, what is your system's configuration?
- On shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io> I also see a delay of about 25 s to load the map. (This is the time after the initial server startup time.) This is what I am seeing today, but I know on Tuesday (Oct 28th) I was seeing much worse behavior from your application. But we figured out there was a problem on shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io> that day. Do you see a difference between Tuesday and today?
- On shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io>, almost any action after the initial load causes your app to crash. I think this is a memory issue. Do you know the size of your application on shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io>?
I monitored memory consumption of your application locally. It takes about 400MB initially when map is loaded. And after that it keeps increasing. The slider at the bottom is the one that uses most memory. I saw memory more than 1G after playing with your app a little bit. So the crash on shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io> might be expected if you are using a small or medium size. Please refer to this guide <http://shiny.rstudio-staging.com/articles/shinyapps.html>, section on "Configuring applications" on how to change the size of application. But you should also look into making your application more efficient.

Best,
Fereshteh

